d1-omni Decide Android sample

Model: d1-omni-600M by Liquid AI, Inc. (huggingface.co/LiquidAI/d1-omni-600M, revision
414f8d6438174f5b2133a9c21a478fc42625e308), licensed under the LFM Open License v1.0 (LICENSE,
unchanged). The LiteRT graphs, contract.json, tokenizer.json and host/vision_position_table.npy the
app loads come from the model repository litert-community/d1-omni-600M-LiteRT, a converted and
modified Derivative Work of that model whose NOTICE lists the changes (decision graphs per
input-length bucket, the vision tower and projector, audio encoders per clip-length bucket, fp16
fully connected weights, fp16-safe normalisation layers). They are installed on the device, not kept
in this source tree.

The request handling is a Kotlin port of the provider's prompt.py (same revision, file sha256
a6b29a55ec8345f1fc1fdbfcc4b64d80d473dc4316f095a62c51cb6cce1194cf), LFM Open License v1.0:
as_question, escape, serialize, _criterion, render_options, encode, answer and temperature_key
(app/src/main/java/com/d1omni/D1Prompt.kt), and of the model repository's Python host
(host/d1_omni.py and host/d1_host.py): each request kind's settings, build_inputs, the bucket choice
and readout_f64 (D1Rows.kt, D1Readout.kt). Changes: Python's json.dumps and str() and CPython 3.12's
float sum are reproduced in Kotlin; the read-out runs in float64 as readout_f64 does; the graphs run
on LiteRT CompiledModel on the GPU, the decision graphs at FP32 and the audio graph, the vision tower
and the projector at FP16_WITH_FP32_ACCUM (launch extras select others; the CPU when the GPU cannot
compile or run a graph).

The audio path is a Kotlin port of the model repository's Python host host/d1_audio_host.py (the
provider's audio.py at the same revision, LFM Open License v1.0): waveform, the preemphasis, the Hann
window, the STFT, the Slaney mel filter bank, the log and the per-bin normalization, the lengths and
buckets, build_inputs and prefix_rows (D1Audio.kt), and of read_audio for 16 kHz mono PCM16 wav files
(D1Wav.kt). Changes: the mel runs every step in float64 and rounds to float32 once at the end (the
host's float64 form; the provider computes in float32), with a radix-2 FFT of its own. The picture
path is a Kotlin port of host/d1_vision_host.py (the provider's vision.py layout and preprocessing and
transformers' position-table resize; D1Vision.kt, D1Image.kt).

app/src/main/res/raw/sample_voice_note.wav is speech synthesised with Kokoro-82M (hexgrad/Kokoro-82M,
revision f3ff3571, Apache License 2.0, licenses/Kokoro-82M-APACHE-2.0.txt) in the voice
am_michael from a line written for this sample. app/src/main/res/raw/img_dogs_01.png is a CC0 1.0 photograph
from Wikimedia Commons (File:Two_French_bulldogs_swimming_in_life_jackets.jpg, long side resized to 384 px), the
model repository's public check-set file (fixtures/media/). The message, the questions and the pet-grooming shop
in app/src/main/res/raw/sample.json are invented for this sample.

The app's own steps around the ported code: a picture longer than 384 px on its long side is shrunk to 384 px
with the provider's float bilinear antialias resize before the provider's preprocessing (D1Decide.kt, D1Photo);
a recording is taken from the microphone at 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM and saved as a wav file (D1Recorder.kt,
D1Wav.encode).

The tokenizer follows the published tokenizer.json contract of Hugging Face tokenizers and
transformers (Apache License 2.0; licenses/Tokenizers-APACHE-2.0.txt and
licenses/Transformers-APACHE-2.0.txt): added-token extraction (the tokens marked normalized: false,
then those marked normalized: true), the Split pre-tokenizer regex, the ByteLevel mapping and
byte-level BPE. D1Json.kt and D1Tokenizer.kt are adapted from this repository's kev sample (Apache
License 2.0, the text in licenses/Tokenizers-APACHE-2.0.txt).

Gradle wrapper files retain their upstream Apache License 2.0 headers.
